WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.703
The crosswalk follows one design rule
above all: use a native Entra attribute

2
00:00:04.703 --> 00:00:09.138
wherever one exists, because other
Microsoft features already read them.

3
00:00:09.138 --> 00:00:14.460
Extensions come in only where a dynamic
membership rule can't read the native value,

4
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.392
and that's a real gap:
rules can't see worker type,

5
00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:19.475
the org data block or the manager.

6
00:00:19.475 --> 00:00:23.125
So three extension attributes
carry codes for access:

7
00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:26.450
organization, worker type
and position category.

8
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.620
They exist in both Active
Directory and Entra ID,

9
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.850
so a rule works the same for hybrid and
cloud users through years of coexistence.

10
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.562
And they hold codes, never display names.

11
00:00:37.562 --> 00:00:41.090
Next, the rest of the slots,
and who may write them.
